+# Board A, round 4: hardware/firmware contract items (MESHSAT-1357, 26 September 2026)
+
+Items this round's board A changes hand to firmware, for W5's `w5-hw-fw-contract.md` (the integrator merges). Each
+names the part, the register or line, the value, the reason and the source. None is built or tested: every one is
+NOT_YET_TESTED and several need a bench reading.
+
+| ID | Part / line | Firmware duty | Why | Source |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| FW-A01 | BQ25731 U3, ChargeOption1 RSNS_RAC | Write RSNS_RAC = 0b **first**, before any input-current setting | R16 (RAC) is 10 mOhm; the POR default 1b assumes 5 mOhm, so every input-current figure reads half the true current until it is written | SLUSE66A 9.3.5; A02 section 5; W2 F-CH-05 |
+| FW-A02 | BQ25731 ChargeCurrent (REG 0x03/02) | At most **3.0 A** for the 4S3P 35E pack (the nearest register code at or below it), lower as the gauge's temperature and state of charge ask | three cells in parallel at the 35E's 1,020 mA cycle-life charge current is 3.06 A; the old 4 A design setting was above it (S-20, D-06) | samsung-35e-orbtronic.pdf 3.5; W2 runtime section 8 |
+| FW-A03 | BQ25731 watchdog | Keep WDTMR_ADJ enabled and service it; decide the value to leave on a crash (with the S-04 topology a host-free charger still carries the kit from shore, and ChargeCurrent governs only the pack) | after S-04 the 256 mA POR default is a real trickle into the pack and shore carries the load up to the input limit; the watchdog returns ChargeCurrent to 256 mA, not 0 (TI E2E 1316778) | A02 sections 1 and 4 |
