ack and with it off: VIN_RAW's current through board E's LM5069 (no current-limit event, no fault retry), VBUS20's ramp time against the 0.41 to 1.29 s of C7 = 4.7 uF (fourth fix-up), when the charger's CHRG_OK rises and its converter starts relative to FE_PGOOD, and the VINDPM value the charger detected (REG 0x0B/0A read back) (`r4-decisions.md` section 6 B4, FW-A16); and THE RESTART INTO A CHARGED VBUS20 (fourth fix-up, R4A-N15): with VBUS20 charged at 18.5 and 20.7 V, dips of 1, 10, 50, 100 and 200 ms below the restart guard's UV (8.08 V nominal) and a full removal, at 12 V and 24 V: VIN_RAW's peak (the guard's pass criterion is no rise above the vehicle's own level beyond a few volts), the FE's inductor current (a current probe on L1: no reverse excursion beyond the few amperes of a start from under 0.8 V), FE_RUN's hold time and VBUS20's bleed curve against 0.64 to 1.17 s to 0.78 V, the level VBUS20 is released at, any LM5069 current-limit or retry event on board E, and the same for a dip that stays above the UV (the stage must ride through with no FE_RUN edge); (11) a charger load release (fourth fix-up, R4A-N16, O-32): at 12 V and 24 V from the vehicle and at full charge power, CHG_INHIBIT asserted, then a PA key-up at IIN_DPM: VBUS20's overshoot, the FE's reverse current, VIN_RAW's peak against the 36 V service maximum and board E's 40 V OVLO, any OVLO or clamp event, and whether the guard then held and restarted the stage | | TEST-PLAN (W5) |
+| FW-A16 | BQ25731 U3 IIN_HOST (REG 0x0F/0E) and InputVoltage (REG 0x0B/0A); board E's VIN_MON (the sensor controller's ADC, over USB) | (a) Hold the charger's input at or under 80 percent of board E's guaranteed vehicle entry at the present VIN_RAW: IIN_HOST at or below 0.80 x 4.80 A x 0.93 x VIN_RAW / 20.7 V, which is 1.55 A at 9 V, 1.73 A at 10 V, 2.07 A at 12 V, 2.38 A at 13.8 V, 2.76 A at 16 V and 4.14 A at 24 V; from about 25 V (4.3 A) to 33 V (5.7 A) the front end's own ISNS limit takes over. VIN_RAW is read from board E's VIN_MON; while it is unknown, use the 9 V figure. (b) While on the pack with no adapter present, write IIN_HOST to the 9 V figure, so a vehicle arriving at any voltage starts inside the entry: the charger resets IIN_HOST to 3.25 A at every adapter removal (SLUSE66A 9.3.6), which is 8.0 A at board E's entry at 9 V and 6.0 A at 12 V (VBUS20 at 20.7 V, efficiency 0.93). (c) Once VBUS20 is in regulation (FE_PGOOD high, U28 pin 20), write InputVoltage (VINDPM) to about 18.5 V: the charger sets its default VINDPM from VBUS "at no load right before the converter is enabled" (9.3.6), and with the front end's 0.3 to 0.9 s soft start that measurement can land mid-ramp. (d) FW-A01's RSNS_RAC = 0b comes first, since every IIN_HOST figure above is at the 10 mOhm scale. When the panel's tracker feeds too, the bus can carry more than the entry (the tracker's 6.16 A is ORed in behind the hot-swap), but VIN_MON cannot tell the two sources apart, so this rule stays at the vehicle's figure. THE CONSEQUENCE, stated (fourth fix-up, the third re-review's minor item 2): with only the panel feeding, IIN_HOST is held at the vehicle's figure for the tracker's 15.1 V, 0.8 x 4.80 x 0.93 x 15.1 / 20.7 = 2.61 A, about 54 W at the charger's input against TRK_OUT's 93 W, and vehicle plus panel together is capped at the vehicle's figure: a charge-power reduction on a D-01 core function, recorded as the reduction it is (O-33). It lifts when board E routes the tracker's TRK_IMONO or PV_P's level to the sensor controller, so this rule can add the tracker's share | Board E's LM5069 U6 (R19 10 mOhm) limits the vehicle entry at VCL 48.5 / 55 / 61.5 mV, 4.85 to 6.15 A, 4.80 A with R19's 1 percent; the front end is a constant-power load, so once U6 limits, VIN_RAW collapses to the stage's UVLO and the stage restarts (since the fourth fix-up that UVLO is the restart guard's UV, 7.86 to 8.31 V falling, and the restart waits for VBUS20's bleed, R4A-N15). The 80 percent leaves the soft start's own share (11.2 percent at 9 V with the third fix-up's 3.3 uF, 8.6 percent with the fourth fix-up's 4.7 uF, `drafts/scripts/softstart.py`) and a margin of about 9 percent at every VIN_RAW. Host-free at POR (RSNS_RAC 1b, IIN_HOST 3.2 A against the 10 mOhm R16) the charger is limited to 1.72 A, 88.6 percent of the entry at 9 V by itself (R4A-N10) | board E F-IN-02 (gen_sch_e.py on main faf8c981: "it sets what the host may ask"); SLUSE66A 9.3.1, 9.3.6, 9.6.22; `r4-decisions.md` section 6 B4 |
